##  The 2-Minute GIT  Cheat Sheet
Think of Git as a time-travel camera for your cloud files.
## 🟢 Phase 1: The Setup

* git init: Turns a regular folder into a Git repository. Installs the time machine.
* git config: Sets your name and email. Signs your name on every save.

## 🟡 Phase 2: The Daily Loop (Saving Work)

* git status: Shows what files changed. Your project dashboard.
* git add .: Stages your files. Puts your changes on the launchpad.
* git commit -m "message": Saves your changes permanently. Clicks the camera shutter to take a snapshot.
* git log --oneline: Lists your past saves. Your history logbook.

## 🌿 Phase 3: Safe Experiments (Branching)

* git checkout -b <name>: Creates and switches to a new branch. Creates an isolated playground so you don't break working code.
* git checkout main: Switches back to the master timeline. Leaves your playground and goes back to the live app code.
* git branch -d <name>: Deletes a branch. Safely throws away the playground when you are finished.

## ☁️ Phase 4: The Cloud (GitHub)

* git remote add origin <URL>: Links your laptop to GitHub. Builds the bridge to the cloud.
* git push origin <name>: Uploads your local branch. Sends your snapshots to GitHub.
* git pull origin main: Downloads the latest code from GitHub. Updates your laptop with your team's changes.

## 🛡️ The Secret Guard

* .gitignore: A hidden text file. Tells Git which secret files (like passwords and cloud keys) to completely ignore and never upload.


